# LSP 5th Deep-Dive Findings Detail — 2026-09-02
# File: openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_09_02_5th_deepdive_findings.oot
# Companion to: lsp_redteam_2026_09_02_5th_deepdive.oot (226 lines, under cap)

# ## 0. Methodology: reviewed all 32 .oo files + LSP_SETUP.oot. Cross-referenced
# every public function definition against actual call sites via grep across the
# full openOODA tree. Found 3 broken refs, 1 dup, 1 compat stub, 4 prefix
# families, 26+ dead fns, 5+ dup utilities, 3 re-introduced heuristics, 1 manual
# struct pattern, 9+ stale doc-drift items, 6 other minor findings.

# ## 1. CRITICAL — BROKEN BUILD
#
# C1: lsp_server_build_index undefined
#   Location: ooda/lsp/lsp_stdio.oo:90, 114. Post-rename audit said it was a
#   duplicate of lsp_server_refresh_index and should be deleted; the function WAS
#   removed from lsp_server_handlers.oo but the two call sites in lsp_stdio.oo
#   were never updated. Every `ooda lsp` invocation fails. The build is broken.
#   Fix: replace both call sites with lsp_server_refresh_index(fs, env, explicit_root).
#
# C2: lsp_compile_scan_user not imported
#   Location: ooda/lsp/lsp_hover.oo:227. The function is defined in
#   ooda/oodac/api_lsp.oo:60, NOT imported by lsp_hover.oo. When
#   lsp_hover_via_compiler is exercised, this fails.
#   Fix: move lsp_compile_scan_user to ooda/lsp/lsp_compile.oo, add import.
#
# C3: lsp_index_from_module undefined
#   Location: ooda/lsp/lsp_stdlib_scan.oo:174. Referenced but defined nowhere.
#   lsp_scan_via_compiler depends on it.
#   Fix: implement in lsp_compiler_merge.oo (extract lsp_compiler_merge_into_index
#   logic into a from-module conversion).

# ## 2. STALE COMPAT LAYER
#
# S1: ooda/oodac/api_lsp.oo is a parallel stub LSP bridge (89 lines)
#   Duplicates all 7 Lsp* struct defs from ooda/lsp/lsp_types_symbol.oo.
#   Stub lsp_compile_module (line 26-31) returns empty after checks, no walk.
#   Stub lsp_compile_residual (line 79-84) returns list_new() after checks.
#   Real lsp_compile_scan_user (line 60-78) — the ONLY real function. Belongs in
#   lsp_compile.oo. 5 trivial lsp_module_*_count getters (line 85-89) are
#   list_len wrappers.
#   TIME BOMB: any caller importing oodac/api_lsp.oo gets the STUB
#   lsp_compile_module, not the real one. The shadow will silently break the LSP
#   if a test or external tool imports the wrong layer.
#   Fix: delete oodac/api_lsp.oo entirely. Move lsp_compile_scan_user to
#   ooda/lsp/lsp_compile.oo (also fixes C2).

# ## 3. DUPLICATE FUNCTION DEFINITION
#
# D1: lsp_module_empty is defined in 2 files (identical signature + body)
#   - ooda/lsp/lsp_compile.oo:18 AND ooda/lsp/lsp_types_symbol.oo:29.
#   Both: pub fn lsp_module_empty(uri: String) -> LspModuleSymbolTable returning
#   the empty struct with list_new() for all 6 collection fields.
#   Fix: delete from lsp_compile.oo (canonical is lsp_types_symbol.oo).

# ## 4. PREFIX-MISMATCH FAMILIES (4 more, missed by 3rd pass)
#
# P1: ooda/lsp/lsp_code_action.oo has 2 lsp_json_* helpers
#   lsp_json_skip_ws (15), lsp_json_first_array_object (29). Both used only by
#   lsp_code_action_resolve. The lsp_json_ prefix is wrong — there's no
#   lsp_json.oo file. Fix: rename to lsp_code_action_*.
#
# P2: ooda/lsp/lsp_definition.oo has 9 lsp_def_* functions
#   lsp_def_starts_with (18, wrapper), lsp_def_format_location (22),
#   lsp_def_builtin_path (31), lsp_def_is_builtin (46), lsp_def_resolve (50),
#   lsp_def_response_json (58), lsp_def_resolve_compiler (65),
#   lsp_def_find_line (87), lsp_def_line_end (103).
#   All should be lsp_definition_* per the prefix = file name rule.
#   Fix: rename 9 functions to lsp_definition_* and update call sites.
#
# P3: ooda/lsp/lsp_formatting.oo has 4 lsp_server_* functions (incomplete rename)
#   lsp_server_normalize_indent (15), lsp_server_handle_formatting (50),
#   lsp_server_extract_doc_symbols (59), lsp_server_handle_document_symbol (96).
#   The FILE was renamed lsp_server_helpers.oo → lsp_formatting.oo but the
#   function prefixes were not updated. lsp_server_* belongs in server dispatch.
#   Fix: rename 4 functions to lsp_formatting_*.
#
# P4: ooda/lsp/lsp_generational.oo has 10 lsp_gen_* functions
#   lsp_gen_from_compiler (16), lsp_gen_badge_via_compiler (30), lsp_gen_label (35),
#   lsp_gen_aircraft (46), lsp_gen_badge (57), lsp_gen_has_gen1_marker (61),
#   lsp_gen_is_violation (77), lsp_gen_violation_msg (83),
#   lsp_gen_violation_diagnostic (87), lsp_gen_publish_diagnostics (94),
#   lsp_gen_badge_with_diagnostic (103).
#   Fix: rename 10 to lsp_generational_* (combine with X2 dead removal).

# ## 5. DEAD CODE (26+ functions across 4 files)
#
# X1: ooda/lsp/lsp_diagnostics.oo — 14 DEAD (file is 50% dead, 81→~35 lines)
#   Form a dead subgraph rooted at lsp_maneuver_collect_live and
#   lsp_maneuver_collect_diagnostics. The live code path uses
#   lsp_server_extract_diags in lsp_server_handlers.oo, which calls only
#   lsp_maneuver_weight_to_diagnostic, lsp_maneuver_pins_to_diagnostic,
#   lsp_maneuver_ps_to_diagnostic, lsp_maneuver_concat_diags,
#   lsp_gen_violation_diagnostic. Everything else is dead.
#   DEAD (line numbers): 33, 34, 40, 48, 49, 50, 51, 52, 62, 63, 64, 71, 74, 76.
#   Fix: delete 14 dead functions.
#
# X2: ooda/lsp/lsp_generational.oo — 2 DEAD
#   lsp_gen_publish_diagnostics (94), lsp_gen_badge_with_diagnostic (103).
#   lsp_gen_violation_diagnostic (87) is alive (called by lsp_server_handlers.oo:53).
#   Fix: delete 2 dead functions.
#
# X3: ooda/lsp/lsp_maneuver.oo — 5 DEAD
#   lsp_maneuver_ps_info (21): returns static string. Academy header documents it.
#   lsp_maneuver_gauge (31): "Ps=X..." string. Diagnostic version is alive.
#   lsp_maneuver_caps_text (36): static string. Constants exported as Int already.
#   lsp_maneuver_gauge_live (112): "Ps=X..." string with live data. Diagnostic is alive.
#   lsp_maneuver_v_default (120): returns 10. Hardcoded 10 in lsp_server_handlers.oo:57.
#   Fix: delete 5 dead functions. File shrinks 140→~110 lines.
#
# X4: ooda/lsp/lsp_facade.oo — 5 DEAD (file is 83% dead, 31→6 lines)
#   lsp_cap_text (20), lsp_cap_input (21), lsp_cap_msgs (22): 1-line aliases.
#   lsp_frame_message (24): 1-line alias.
#   lsp_query_hover (28): hardcoded id="1" call. Never used.
#   ALIVE: lsp_version (18) — used by lsp_extras.oo:107 and lsp_double_run_v2.oo:30,31.
#   Per the "no re-export layers" directive, lsp_facade.oo is a FACADE.
#   Fix: delete lsp_facade.oo. Move lsp_version into mod.oo (mod_lsp_version).

# ## 6. DUPLICATE TEXT UTILITIES (lsp_text.oo not adopted)
#
# T1: ooda/lsp/lsp_hover.oo has 3 duplicates of lsp_text.oo
#   lsp_hover_line (113), lsp_hover_line_start (96), lsp_hover_trim (124).
#   Plus lsp_hover_starts_with (26) is a 1-line wrapper for str_starts_with.
#   Fix: replace with lsp_text.oo. Shrinks lsp_hover.oo by ~40 lines.
#
# T2: ooda/lsp/lsp_definition.oo has 1 wrapper + 2 line-scanner duplicates
#   lsp_def_starts_with (18), lsp_def_line_end (103), lsp_def_find_line (87).
#   Fix: remove wrapper, use lsp_text.oo utilities.
#
# T3: ooda/lsp/lsp_stdio.oo has lsp_skip_ws (25) — 13-line whitespace skipper.
#   Also `fn` (not `pub fn`), wrong access. Move to lsp_text.oo.
#
# T4: ooda/lsp/lsp_code_action.oo has lsp_json_skip_ws (15) — same 13-line pattern.
#   Use lsp_text_skip_ws from lsp_text.oo.
#
# T5: ooda/lsp/lsp_stdlib_scan.oo has 3 hand-rolled utilities
#   lsp_scan_ends_with (18): str_ends_with is a built-in. STALE FIX.
#   lsp_scan_skip_ws (58): 9-line whitespace skipper.
#   lsp_scan_match_at (82): substring match check; could be 1 line.

# ## 7. RE-INTRODUCED HEURISTIC FALLBACKS
#
# H1: ooda/lsp/lsp_maneuver.oo:67, 73 — D_alloc/D_search substring counters
#   Count "heap"+"alloc" and "token_burn"+"search" substrings. Same antipattern
#   as the removed lsp_gen_from_path. Compiler can give real counts.
#   A comment containing "realloc" inflates the drag diagnostic. Fix: replace
#   with real counts from lsp_compile_walk_fns output, or remove.
#
# H2: ooda/lsp/lsp_maneuver.oo:53 — ast_weight substring counter
#   Counts "pub fn "/etc substrings. Same antipattern. Fix: replace with
#   lsp_compile_walk_fns output.
#
# H3: ooda/lsp/lsp_generational.oo:16 — package→Gen if-else table
#   Function name says "from_compiler" but the mapping is a hardcoded if-else
#   chain. Per STRUCTURE_EM.oot 3.4, Gen should come from the compiler.
#   Fix: extend LspModuleSymbolTable with gen field, populated by
#   lsp_compile_walk_* based on ooda.pkg metadata.
#
# H4: ooda/lsp/lsp_generational.oo:61 — chain of 13 str_index_of for Gen1 markers
#   Data table masquerading as code. Fix: replace with List[String] of markers
#   + a single str_index_of_any.

# ## 8. MANUAL STRUCT CONSTRUCTION
#
# M1: ooda/lsp/lsp_compile.oo — 8 manual struct constructions
#   Lines 52, 53, 68, 70, 86, 87, 102, 103 manually construct LspFunction,
#   LspStruct, LspEnum, LspCapabilityUse with all 8 fields spelled out. The
#   constructors lsp_function_new, lsp_struct_new, lsp_enum_new, lsp_cap_use_new
#   exist in lsp_types_symbol.oo but are not used. Every manual construction
#   has a 1-line constructor equivalent. Saves 20+ lines of repetition.

