# ## 10. OTHER FINDINGS
#
# O1: ooda/lsp/mod.oo:16, 17 — duplicate import of lsp_stdio.oo. Delete one.
#
# O2: ooda/lsp/lsp_completion.oo:40 — lsp_completion_via_compiler doesn't use
#   the compiler. Body uses no CompilerReadCap. Rename to lsp_completion_respond
#   or add the compiler parameter and use it.
#
# O3: ooda/lsp/lsp_formatting.oo:86 — hardcoded "file://x" URI and kind:12.
#   "file://x" is a placeholder URI. kind:12 is LSP SymbolKind.Function. Pass
#   uri as parameter; use named constant for kind:12.
#
# O4: ooda/lsp/lsp_diagnostics.oo:46 — hardcoded end_col: 80. Magic line width.
#   Name the constant lsp_em_diag_line_width.
#
# O5: ooda/lsp/lsp_diagnostics.oo:48 — code-by-substring-search antipattern.
#   Diagnostic code derived from substring search on the message. If the
#   message text changes, the code lookup breaks. Fix: have
#   lsp_maneuver_drag_live_diag return the code along with the message.
#
# O6: ooda/lsp/lsp_maneuver.oo:122 — lsp_maneuver_count_substr is O(n*m).
#   17 lines of hand-rolled counter. If str_count_of exists, use it.

# ## 11. E-M delta
#
# Ps_pre  (post-4-passes) = (T_nominal - D_3_broken + 26_dead + 4_prefix +
#                            5_dup + 3_heuristic + 1_compat) / W * V ≈ 0
# Ps_post (post-5th-pass) = (T_real - D_~0) / 3126 * HIGH >> 0
# Each broken ref is W=0 fail-closed. Each dead fn adds 0 to Ps but inflates W.
